            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 24 manifest paths for security, data loss and unsafe input handling; no reachable candidate-caused risk found.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: PlanUninstall refuses a procedural id or an id with no install record before planning. It then reuses install's planSkill, so an edited, non-regular or unreadable recorded file refuses the whole uninstall with nothing removed. The id from the command line only selects a record and is never used as a path.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: removeEmptyTree calls Remove only on directories that hold nothing but empty directories. It deletes no file and does not follow symlinks, so files the install record does not list are preserved and their directory is reported as kept.",
              "engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go: uninstall takes the exclusive project lock on the absolute working directory before any read or write, and refuses before locking when the working directory is not absolute. A dry run writes nothing.",
              "Whether recorded paths in an install record are confined to the project is decided by the base planner, which this patch neither shows nor changes, so I report nothing on it.",
              "The project-status change only adds read-only output lines. The retryVerb change keeps the 'run install again' wording for install and adopt. The remaining files are docs, goldens, tests and review receipts with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
