            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R4-kept-note-misleading",
                "lens": "resilience",
                "location": "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go:76-86",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "RemoveEmptySkillDirs is best effort and reports any directory it cannot read or remove as kept. The CLI then prints 'note: kept \u003cdir\u003e: it holds files skills install did not write', which is inaccurate for a permission or I/O failure. Exit is 0 and the record is already gone, so the operator is told the wrong cause and a rerun cannot clean it up because the install record no longer exists. The impact is a leftover empty directory with a misleading message, not data loss. The lines are in a new file and the code was already carried as a follow-up in the task note.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go:76-86",
                  "engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go:124-126"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 24 manifest paths for failure handling, retry safety, graceful degradation, observability, latency and load. I found no candidate-caused BLOCKER or CRITICAL failure mode.",
              "Refusals (edited file, non-regular file, unreadable file, no install record, procedural id) all come from the planner before ExecuteInstallPlan runs, so nothing is removed on refusal. engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go compare the tree before and after.",
              "Retry safety: a recorded file that is already gone is tolerated by the plan, so a rerun after a partial execution failure can finish the uninstall. The install record is dropped only as part of the executed plan.",
              "Concurrency: uninstall takes the exclusive project lock through ProjectLocks and releases it with defer. A relative working directory is refused before locking.",
              "Dry run writes nothing, and the output states that the lock file stays. The earlier misreport of the lock file in the plan was fixed in this candidate.",
              "Load: work is proportional to the number of files in one install record, with no network or registry reads.",
              "The receipts, README, usage text, golden files and task note have no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
