            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 24 manifest paths for behavior, failure paths, determinism and test coverage. I found no candidate-caused BLOCKER or CRITICAL reliability defect.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go reuses install's planner via planSkill, so an edited, non-regular or unreadable recorded file, an id with no install record, or a procedural id refuses the whole uninstall before any removal. engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go assert the tree is unchanged after each refusal.",
              "The dry run in engine/skills/app/uninstall.go writes nothing. engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go prints one 'plan: remove' line per file and a lock update line saying the file stays, and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go pins that output and the unchanged tree.",
              "Recorded files already gone, a missing runtime directory, and unrecorded files (kept with their directory) are covered by tests in engine/skills/uninstall_plan_test.go and engine/cmd/skills_uninstall_cli_test.go.",
              "engine/skills/lock.go makes the uninstall project lock exclusive and takes no overlay lock; the CLI test checks both, and a relative working directory is refused before locking with no lock file created.",
              "The project-status change in engine/skills/app/project.go lists install records and lets the id filter match either kind. 'Not in lock' fires only when neither matches, and the CLI test covers listing, filtering, unknown id and the state after uninstall.",
              "The retry hint in engine/skills/install_plan_skill.go names the running verb; install and adopt keep 'run install again', so baseline output is preserved. The argv goldens change only in the verb list."
